        "name": "USN-8166-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that RetroArch did not correctly handle certain memory operations, which could lead to a buffer overflow. If a user or automated system were tricked into opening a specially crafted file, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. This issue only affected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 25.10.",
